    <string name="meditation_intro_text">Relax. Sit comfortably. Feel your breath. Let your thoughts slow down. This time is just for you.</string>
    <string name="guidance_prompt_soft_inhale_exhale">Take a gentle inhale through your nose… and a slow exhale.</string>
    <string name="guidance_prompt_release_shoulders">Notice your shoulders releasing tension.</string>
    <string name="guidance_prompt_focus_chest">Focus on sensations in the chest area.</string>
    <string name="guidance_prompt_belly_breath">Let the belly rise as you inhale and fall as you exhale.</string>
    <string name="guidance_prompt_return_attention">If distracted — gently return to your breath.</string>
    <string name="meditation_about_text">Meditation is a practice of mindfulness and relaxation. It helps reduce stress, improve focus and sleep. Start with 5–10 minutes, breathe evenly, observe sensations.</string>
    <string name="meditation_how_to_text">Sit comfortably with a straight back. Close your eyes. Breathe calmly. Do not try to “turn off thoughts” — simply observe. If you drift, gently return to your breath.</string>
    <string name="breathing_how_help_text">Increases heart rate variability, improves focus, accelerates relaxation. Recommended 2–3 times a day for 3–5 minutes.</string>

